1
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:11,633
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,367 --> 00:00:32,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:34,933
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:40,767
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,733
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:45,067
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:46,633
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,633 --> 00:00:47,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:50,967
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:53,500
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,367
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,800
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,867
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,533
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,967 --> 00:01:08,933
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,467 --> 00:01:12,833
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:14,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:21,033
<i> Guys, don't blow your cover.</i>

21
00:01:21,033 --> 00:01:22,367
<i> We need to find Sam.</i>

22
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:24,433
<i> Hey! Stop it!</i>

23
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:27,067
<i> Sir, it feels like...</i>

24
00:01:27,067 --> 00:01:29,267
<i>...the work of the thugs
of Ginintuang Lupa!</i>

25
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:31,567
<i>- I need to talk to your son.
- I'll tell him.</i>

26
00:01:31,567 --> 00:01:33,600
<i>I'll have him finish
what he started.</i>

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:35,633
<i>Doesn't it seem
like you're rushing this?</i>

28
00:01:35,633 --> 00:01:38,000
<i>Max, we're not abandoning
the search for Sam.</i>

29
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,633
<i>But we also cannot abandon
our land.</i>

30
00:01:40,667 --> 00:01:43,633
<i>There are some people outside
who want to talk to you.</i>

31
00:01:43,633 --> 00:01:46,633
<i>We're here again to try
to settle this...</i>

32
00:01:46,633 --> 00:01:48,767
<i>It's Max.
What is she doing here?</i>

33
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:51,367
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:52,733
Alright, have a seat.

35
00:01:53,967 --> 00:01:55,100
Have a seat, Attorney.

36
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:08,100
[MAMENG]
What exactly do you want?

37
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:10,600
We're here to offer to settle

38
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:13,533
after the incident that happened
during the demolition.

39
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:17,300
[MAMENG] We just want to know
who shot Rudy.

40
00:02:17,333 --> 00:02:19,200
Once we find out who shot him,

41
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:23,667
we'll then file a case
against that person.

42
00:02:23,667 --> 00:02:28,833
We actually came here
to help you with that.

43
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:29,933
Help?

44
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:33,033
You just said
you're here to settle.

45
00:02:33,033 --> 00:02:34,467
If you want to settle,

46
00:02:34,467 --> 00:02:37,567
that means there has
to be a lawsuit, am I right?

47
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:38,767
[CLEARS THROAT]

48
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:40,600
You haven't filed a case

49
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:43,800
and there's still no suspect
in who shot Mister Rudy.

50
00:02:44,567 --> 00:02:45,567
Uh, babes,

51
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:48,067
who are we suing then?

52
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,267
The cops, of course.

53
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:51,533
The cops shot Rudy.

54
00:02:51,533 --> 00:02:53,333
That's your hunch.

55
00:02:53,333 --> 00:02:55,267
You still don't have proof

56
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:57,833
that cops shot Mister Rudy.

57
00:02:57,833 --> 00:02:58,833
Uh, Mameng.

58
00:02:59,467 --> 00:03:02,600
The way I see it,
they could be right.

59
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:06,300
We don't know
who we're going to sue.

60
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:11,400
This can help us recover
from the hospital bills we paid.

61
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:14,267
We can't just pass this up.

62
00:03:14,267 --> 00:03:16,133
Betchay, that's not
the way to go.

63
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:20,533
I'll find out who among
those cops shot me,

64
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,900
all because
of Ricardo Jacinto's orders!

65
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,667
I know who I'm going to sue!

66
00:03:29,667 --> 00:03:33,767
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

67
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:36,233
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]

68
00:03:36,233 --> 00:03:37,933
- [IBYANG] Hold on, let's...
- Django.

69
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:39,100
Pa.

70
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,100
Boss Mariano called me.

71
00:03:42,033 --> 00:03:43,400
What did he say?

72
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,500
- Does he want something done?
- He'll have you picked up.

73
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:48,533
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:52,233
I told you, Pa,
I'll bounce back.

75
00:03:52,233 --> 00:03:56,333
I have a chance to show
the Zafras what I'm capable of.

76
00:03:56,367 --> 00:03:57,700
Just make sure

77
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:01,433
you and your men
don't mess up again.

78
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:05,667
I'll stick to the plan
to make Gabo the fall guy.

79
00:04:05,667 --> 00:04:07,900
[LAUGHS EVILLY]

80
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:09,767
Oh.

81
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:12,933
But you failed to convince Gabo
to return to the group.

82
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:15,733
He doesn't have to be with us
to take the fall.

83
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,433
I already came up with a plan.

84
00:04:21,533 --> 00:04:22,800
And I'll make it happen.

85
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,833
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:28,100
Oh, Rudy, don't be so rash.

87
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:31,633
We might lose in this.
We can't afford a lawyer.

88
00:04:32,767 --> 00:04:35,200
[ROWENA] That's still up to you.
Mr. Magtibay.

89
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:38,733
If you take this to court,
I'm telling you now,

90
00:04:38,733 --> 00:04:41,533
it'll be a very long process.

91
00:04:41,533 --> 00:04:43,833
And you'll shed a lot of money.

92
00:04:43,833 --> 00:04:45,667
If I were you,

93
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:49,233
I'll accept our offer.

94
00:04:49,233 --> 00:04:51,900
How much is your offer
for the settlement?

95
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:53,000
We're offering help,
not settlement.

96
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,933
Help or settlement, whatever.
How much?

97
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:56,700
200,000 pesos.

98
00:05:03,233 --> 00:05:04,433
Oh, that's not enough.

99
00:05:05,567 --> 00:05:08,733
That won't even cover
the hospital bills.

100
00:05:08,733 --> 00:05:10,767
Rudy almost died.

101
00:05:10,767 --> 00:05:13,400
And until now,
he's still on meds.

102
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:16,567
We don't know how we'll
afford it in the coming days.

103
00:05:16,567 --> 00:05:18,667
We can still raise our offer.

104
00:05:18,667 --> 00:05:20,767
How much do you have in mind?

105
00:05:20,767 --> 00:05:22,033
300,000 pesos.

106
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:26,567
That'll cover
all of Rudy's hospital bills.

107
00:05:26,567 --> 00:05:28,300
We'll be able
to pay off our debts

108
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:31,533
and afford his meds.

109
00:05:31,533 --> 00:05:33,200
We're not greedy.

110
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:36,500
We just want an adequate life.

111
00:05:36,533 --> 00:05:38,267
I hear you.

112
00:05:38,267 --> 00:05:40,633
In fact, we already
brought the money.

113
00:05:40,633 --> 00:05:42,200
We have it here.

114
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:45,533
I'm just hoping
you'll sign this document

115
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:48,467
proving we've resolved
our dispute.

116
00:05:48,467 --> 00:05:49,933
No.

117
00:05:49,933 --> 00:05:51,800
My father won't agree to that.

118
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:54,133
We don't want your money!

119
00:05:54,133 --> 00:05:56,100
You better leave
and take that document with you!

120
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,400
Gabo, Gabo. [CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

121
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:00,033
You're doing it again.

122
00:06:00,033 --> 00:06:03,167
Can't you see?
They're offering money.

123
00:06:03,167 --> 00:06:05,000
We can't pass this up.

124
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,467
Betchay, it's not that easy.

125
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,600
And it's not just about money.

126
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,733
You know what, my son is right.

127
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,700
I won't agree to settle

128
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:18,233
and above all,
I won't sign that document!

129
00:06:20,933 --> 00:06:27,533
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:06:27,533 --> 00:06:28,800
Ibyang! Ibyang, there are cops!

131
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:30,500
What?!

132
00:06:31,767 --> 00:06:32,967
Search the whole area!

133
00:06:32,967 --> 00:06:34,133
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

134
00:06:34,133 --> 00:06:35,133
Go, men!

135
00:06:35,933 --> 00:06:37,767
- [COP] Move!
- Django.

136
00:06:37,767 --> 00:06:40,633
I thought NLEA
didn't recognize you?

137
00:06:40,633 --> 00:06:42,000
Why are they here then?

138
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:59,100
Umali, why are you here?

139
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,400
Relax, Paquito.

140
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:02,500
We're just checking around.

141
00:07:02,500 --> 00:07:03,667
What do you need from us?

142
00:07:05,433 --> 00:07:07,967
What are you so mad about, huh?

143
00:07:07,967 --> 00:07:11,800
We're just doing
a standard operating procedure.

144
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,600
- Fernando!
- Sir?

145
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,067
- Open the casket.
- Yes, sir.

146
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,933
[CASKET THUDS]

147
00:07:19,933 --> 00:07:23,167
Umali, have you forgotten
about our agreement?

148
00:07:23,167 --> 00:07:25,233
We need a heads-up!

149
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:27,500
You can't just barge in
like this!

150
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:29,433
It's nothing personal.

151
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:30,433
I'm just doing my job.

152
00:07:30,433 --> 00:07:32,433
Don't go here snooping around!

153
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:34,333
What do you need from us?!

154
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:35,433
Where were you last night?

155
00:07:35,433 --> 00:07:38,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

156
00:07:38,933 --> 00:07:39,967
Speak.

157
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,567
I was here.

158
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,200
You didn't take on
an assignment?

159
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:46,067
Why? Did you have
a mission for me?

160
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:47,700
[SNICKERS]

161
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:49,533
Then the answer's no!

162
00:07:51,133 --> 00:07:52,133
Hey, you.

163
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:54,167
Where were you last night?

164
00:07:54,167 --> 00:07:55,400
I was with Django!

165
00:07:55,733 --> 00:07:56,833
Where?

166
00:07:56,833 --> 00:08:02,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,233
- I knew it!
- Wait, wait!

168
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,233
I knew you were on it!

169
00:08:06,233 --> 00:08:07,600
[PAQUITO] Wait a minute!

170
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:09,233
What exactly do you want?

171
00:08:09,733 --> 00:08:12,067
Sir, we've swept the area!

172
00:08:12,067 --> 00:08:13,100
Negative!

173
00:08:13,767 --> 00:08:15,167
[PAQUITO] Drop your guns.

174
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:17,067
Django.

175
00:08:17,067 --> 00:08:21,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

176
00:08:21,567 --> 00:08:22,733
Paquito.

177
00:08:23,833 --> 00:08:25,433
We've known each other
for a long time.

178
00:08:25,433 --> 00:08:26,600
What I can't stand...

179
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,067
is being betrayed.

180
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,667
[PAQUITO] Umali...

181
00:08:32,667 --> 00:08:34,100
Why would I ever do that?

182
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:36,900
You're always doing us
a big favor.

183
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:38,300
Don't you agree, Django?

184
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:41,300
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:43,367
I'd better not find out
the truth.

186
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,467
Because the moment I learn
you're messing with NLEA,

187
00:08:46,833 --> 00:08:50,367
I'll break
your horns off myself.

188
00:08:52,433 --> 00:08:53,600
Django...

189
00:08:56,367 --> 00:08:57,500
Let's go, men!

190
00:08:58,533 --> 00:08:59,500
Step aside!

191
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:01,333
Yes, sir.

192
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:06,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:09:08,600 --> 00:09:10,100
I think both of you
should leave now.

194
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,033
And please, don't ever show
your faces here again!

195
00:09:13,767 --> 00:09:14,867
Get out!

196
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:17,867
Let's go.
We'll just return another day.

197
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:19,733
Uh, Mr. Magtibay,
we're really sorry.

198
00:09:19,733 --> 00:09:21,233
We'll be on our way now.

199
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,200
Thanks.

200
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:29,333
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:09:29,367 --> 00:09:30,900
I just...

202
00:09:31,333 --> 00:09:32,833
...can't figure you all out.

203
00:09:32,833 --> 00:09:34,400
What the hell were you thinking?

204
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:37,533
Where's that arrogance
coming from?

205
00:09:37,533 --> 00:09:39,400
You're all talk
about principles.

206
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,267
But can that even put food
on the table?

207
00:09:42,233 --> 00:09:43,433
[RUDY HUFFS]

208
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:45,967
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

209
00:09:45,967 --> 00:09:47,067
[MAMENG] Calm down.

210
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:57,833
What are you staring at?
Back to work!

211
00:09:57,833 --> 00:09:58,733
[WOMAN] Come on.

212
00:09:59,633 --> 00:10:00,633
So what now?

213
00:10:00,633 --> 00:10:03,133
NLEA has its eyes on you.

214
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:06,733
Why don't we just cut off
our connection with them?

215
00:10:06,733 --> 00:10:09,167
They're small-time compared
to the Zafras!

216
00:10:09,167 --> 00:10:11,300
Let me remind you both...

217
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:13,867
that this isn't just
about money.

218
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:15,933
They're of some benefit
to us, right?

219
00:10:16,567 --> 00:10:18,900
But we can't drop the Zafras.

220
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:22,267
Who says we have to choose
between the two?

221
00:10:22,267 --> 00:10:24,500
I have to carry out
the Zafras' mission,

222
00:10:24,767 --> 00:10:28,600
all the while keeping NLEA
from investigating us.

223
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:29,600
[SNICKERS]

224
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,800
A wise rat...

225
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:37,000
...never lets itself get trapped
in its own den.

226
00:10:37,033 --> 00:10:41,300
Now is the right time
to set the trap for Gabo.

227
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:46,033
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

228
00:10:46,033 --> 00:10:47,800
I've got an idea, Pa.

229
00:10:58,800 --> 00:10:59,833
Is it true that

230
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:02,167
Reyes and Borromeo
got into a physical altercation

231
00:11:02,167 --> 00:11:04,667
while undercover?

232
00:11:04,667 --> 00:11:07,133
Yes, sir.
I stopped them.

233
00:11:07,133 --> 00:11:08,400
They were out of control!

234
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,367
Good thing I was there.

235
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:12,767
What the hell
were they thinking?

236
00:11:12,767 --> 00:11:16,400
How could they act this way
at a time like this?

237
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:18,333
Exactly, sir.

238
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:20,467
But in our defense, sir,

239
00:11:20,467 --> 00:11:23,233
we've done far more
than that one mishap.

240
00:11:23,233 --> 00:11:24,800
And just so you know,

241
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:27,933
we've given Aunt Isobel Jacinto
some assurance.

242
00:11:27,933 --> 00:11:29,600
Because they know that

243
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:33,333
I am really trying my best
to find their daughter.

244
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:36,100
I do appreciate your effort,
Sebastian.

245
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,633
Thank you.

246
00:11:37,633 --> 00:11:39,933
But I think

247
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:44,867
that won't do much
in our search for Sam.

248
00:11:46,233 --> 00:11:47,800
Not much at all.

249
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:54,800
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,533
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:12:10,533 --> 00:12:11,700
Good morning, sir.

252
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:12,900
Good morning, sir.

253
00:12:12,900 --> 00:12:19,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

254
00:12:31,967 --> 00:12:33,300
Good morning, sir.

255
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,767
Sir Delgado, good morning.

256
00:12:42,133 --> 00:12:49,100
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

257
00:12:50,267 --> 00:12:53,167
Sir, do you need anything?

258
00:12:58,867 --> 00:13:02,700
You are out there
to look for Sam.

259
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:08,300
This... This is our mission,

260
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:10,433
not just for Task Force Alpha,

261
00:13:10,433 --> 00:13:13,100
but for the entire NCIA.

262
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:16,400
I expected better from you.

263
00:13:17,333 --> 00:13:19,033
Get your heads straight.

264
00:13:19,033 --> 00:13:20,367
[INHALES DEEPLY]

265
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:28,567
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

266
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:37,767
That's a lot of money, Rudy.

267
00:13:37,767 --> 00:13:40,367
I've never been offered
that much money before.

268
00:13:40,367 --> 00:13:43,633
Think about it,
300,000 pesos.

269
00:13:43,633 --> 00:13:44,933
Think of what
we could do with it.

270
00:13:44,933 --> 00:13:47,833
We could use it as capital
for the auto repair shop.

271
00:13:47,833 --> 00:13:49,200
Hey, Dante.

272
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,100
That is a lot of money.

273
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:54,000
But that doesn't mean
we should take it.

274
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,300
Uncle Dante,
even though we're poor,

275
00:13:57,333 --> 00:13:59,267
Papa would never
take that money.

276
00:13:59,267 --> 00:14:01,700
I'd rather work until I die

277
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,800
before Papa signs that contract!

278
00:14:05,267 --> 00:14:07,100
I'm sorry, but...

279
00:14:08,033 --> 00:14:10,033
Gabo is right.

280
00:14:10,033 --> 00:14:11,467
Money can be earned,

281
00:14:11,467 --> 00:14:13,900
but life is priceless.

282
00:14:16,033 --> 00:14:17,000
Oh.

283
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:20,900
Look.

284
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,433
They left the document.

285
00:14:23,433 --> 00:14:24,933
- Go after them, Dante.
- Oh, they did.

286
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:26,933
- You can still catch them.
- What?

287
00:14:26,933 --> 00:14:28,300
I don't want to exhaust myself.

288
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:30,567
They'll come back for that.

289
00:14:30,567 --> 00:14:31,900
Can I take a look?

290
00:14:38,833 --> 00:14:40,767
[BETCHAY] Psst!
Hey! Miss Beautiful!

291
00:14:40,767 --> 00:14:43,267
Miss Beautiful, wait!

292
00:14:43,267 --> 00:14:44,767
- Wait a minute.
- [MAXINE CHUCKLES]

293
00:14:44,767 --> 00:14:47,667
- Yes?
- Let's discuss what we can do.

294
00:14:47,667 --> 00:14:51,100
I know I can convince Rudy.

295
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:55,733
That's not what we saw
earlier, Miss Betchay.

296
00:14:55,733 --> 00:14:58,000
Believe me.

297
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,933
All you need is
a signature, right?

298
00:14:59,933 --> 00:15:02,167
Yes, a signature and proof

299
00:15:02,200 --> 00:15:05,000
that he signed
without being coerced.

300
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,767
Oh, that's easy.

301
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:10,167
I can do that.
But of course...

302
00:15:10,167 --> 00:15:11,067
Attorney.

303
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:18,100
Betchay, we'll give you
a down payment, okay?

304
00:15:18,100 --> 00:15:20,100
We will give you
the rest of the money

305
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,133
when you get
the paperwork signed.

306
00:15:22,133 --> 00:15:23,833
We've given you the money.

307
00:15:23,833 --> 00:15:26,333
If the paperwork
doesn't get signed,

308
00:15:26,333 --> 00:15:28,933
you will have to give it back
to us.

309
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,267
Oh, that won't be necessary.

310
00:15:33,267 --> 00:15:36,900
I just need to
talk to Rudy in private

311
00:15:36,933 --> 00:15:40,733
without Gabo, because he
will definitely be against it.

312
00:15:40,733 --> 00:15:43,500
Oh, don't worry about Gabo.

313
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,733
We'll convince him.

314
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:47,333
- Really? Okay.
- Mm-hmm.

315
00:15:47,333 --> 00:15:50,433
Well, if you need help,
just give me a call.

316
00:15:50,433 --> 00:15:52,333
- Thank you very much, Betchay.
- Thank you too.

317
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:54,767
- We'll count on that.
- Yes! Take care.

318
00:15:54,767 --> 00:15:56,333
- Let's go, Attorney.
- Bye.

319
00:15:56,333 --> 00:15:57,400
Okay.

320
00:15:57,400 --> 00:16:04,333
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:16:09,267 --> 00:16:11,733
This is a settlement agreement,
and it won't help you.

322
00:16:11,733 --> 00:16:14,633
If you sign this,
you will lose your property.

323
00:16:14,633 --> 00:16:15,567
[MAMENG] What?!

324
00:16:15,567 --> 00:16:18,100
The lawyer said
it's financial aid.

325
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:20,167
She's lying.

326
00:16:20,167 --> 00:16:21,967
They made the contract difficult
to understand by using English

327
00:16:21,967 --> 00:16:23,267
so you wouldn't know
what it meant.

328
00:16:23,267 --> 00:16:26,667
Pa, if you sign this,
you will lose your home.

329
00:16:28,533 --> 00:16:30,367
Let me see.

330
00:16:36,133 --> 00:16:39,300
Does Betchay know what
the hell we're getting into?!

331
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,733
- Hmm?
- She must know.

332
00:16:40,733 --> 00:16:42,900
That's why
she brought those people here.

333
00:16:43,700 --> 00:16:45,667
Damn you, Betchay!

334
00:16:45,667 --> 00:16:47,400
You are so greedy!

335
00:16:48,567 --> 00:16:51,133
She didn't even think of the
people here at Ginintuang Lupa.

336
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:54,067
She didn't even think about us!

337
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:57,967
[MAMENG] That woman
is willing to compromise

338
00:16:57,967 --> 00:17:02,033
the entire neighborhood
for money.

339
00:17:02,033 --> 00:17:06,700
We're going to lose our home
for a small chunk of money!

340
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:13,400
Auntie, maybe Auntie Betchay
doesn't know that.

341
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:15,233
Maybe they're
deceiving her too.

342
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:20,233
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:17:20,233 --> 00:17:23,633
Betchay, what do you know
about this document?!

344
00:17:23,633 --> 00:17:25,633
Hmm, Betchay?

345
00:17:25,633 --> 00:17:27,033
No, what is that?

346
00:17:27,033 --> 00:17:28,133
Don't play dumb, Betchay.

347
00:17:28,133 --> 00:17:30,233
Do you know what
that document is for?

348
00:17:30,233 --> 00:17:34,233
It says that we will
lose Ginintuang Lupa

349
00:17:34,233 --> 00:17:36,500
the moment Rudy signs that.

350
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:39,200
We'll lose our home!

351
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:42,633
[GABO] Auntie Betchay,
they aren't from an NGO.

352
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:44,200
They're trying to fool us!

353
00:17:45,033 --> 00:17:45,967
What?

354
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:50,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

355
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,600
I don't understand it.
It's in English.

356
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,100
Is that what it says?

357
00:17:55,233 --> 00:17:56,867
Those witches.

358
00:17:58,733 --> 00:18:00,967
They fooled me.

359
00:18:00,967 --> 00:18:02,300
They fooled me!

360
00:18:03,533 --> 00:18:05,267
They will pay for this.

361
00:18:05,267 --> 00:18:06,833
They will pay for this!

362
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:08,433
Mark my words!

363
00:18:08,433 --> 00:18:15,400
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:18:26,067 --> 00:18:27,033
D**n it!

365
00:18:27,567 --> 00:18:28,667
- They're fooling me?
- [ENVELOPE THUMPS]

366
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:31,000
- [BREATHES DEEPLY]
- [PAPER RUSTLES]

367
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,367
You really thought
you could fool me?

368
00:18:32,367 --> 00:18:33,633
[PAPER RUSTLES]

369
00:18:33,633 --> 00:18:36,033
So that's what
this document is about.

370
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:39,200
They're even bribing me!

371
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,200
[MONEY THUMPS]

372
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,367
[ENVELOPE RUSTLES]

373
00:18:41,367 --> 00:18:44,500
Let's see.
Let's see what'll happen to you!

374
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,600
[ENVELOPE SCRAPES, RUSTLES]

375
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:49,700
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

376
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:52,033
[BETCHAY]  That d**n woman.

377
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:54,733
<i> She really chose to fool me?</i>

378
00:18:54,733 --> 00:18:58,033
<i>I thought I was fooling her,
but I was wrong.</i>

379
00:18:58,967 --> 00:19:00,700
<i> She better be ready for me.</i>

380
00:19:02,767 --> 00:19:05,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

381
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,133
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

382
00:19:07,133 --> 00:19:10,767
<i>Miss Pretty, can we meet
at BeerGin later?</i>

383
00:19:10,767 --> 00:19:12,300
[KEYPAD BEEPING]

384
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:15,333
<i>You have no idea
who you're fooling.</i>

385
00:19:15,967 --> 00:19:17,733
[PHONE BUZZING]

386
00:19:17,733 --> 00:19:20,233
"Betchay: Miss Pretty,
can we meet at BeerGin later?"

387
00:19:20,233 --> 00:19:22,800
[BETCHAY] <i> There's something
</i> important I have to tell you.

388
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,500
Attorney, I don't think
her husband will agree.

389
00:19:29,533 --> 00:19:33,233
Ma'am, money talks.

390
00:19:34,367 --> 00:19:36,633
What could our maximum offer be?

391
00:19:37,300 --> 00:19:40,867
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

392
00:19:40,867 --> 00:19:42,900
Attorney, it'd be better
if you start fixing

393
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:44,767
the documents they need to sign.

394
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,067
Get back to me here right away.

395
00:19:48,567 --> 00:19:52,333
We need to make
the residents agree to our plan.

396
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:54,467
Yes, ma'am.

397
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:58,900
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

398
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:01,233
[RUDY] They almost fooled us!

399
00:20:01,233 --> 00:20:06,000
[DANTE] Luckily, we have Gloria.
She got to read the document.

400
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:08,300
Thank you so much, Gloria.

401
00:20:09,533 --> 00:20:12,900
If it weren't for you,
we would've been in trouble.

402
00:20:12,900 --> 00:20:14,633
We might've signed the document

403
00:20:14,633 --> 00:20:18,667
because of the amount
of money they were offering.

404
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:21,567
If possible,
please carefully read

405
00:20:21,567 --> 00:20:23,767
all documents
they're giving you.

406
00:20:23,767 --> 00:20:28,400
If you don't understand it,
you can ask a lawyer.

407
00:20:29,033 --> 00:20:30,567
No matter what...

408
00:20:31,067 --> 00:20:33,433
Don't sign 'cause it wouldn't be
favorable to you.

409
00:20:33,433 --> 00:20:37,300
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:20:37,333 --> 00:20:40,133
Love, thank you so much.

411
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:45,333
You saved us from trouble.

412
00:20:47,367 --> 00:20:49,600
This land is very important
to us.

413
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:52,667
It's our only treasure.

414
00:20:54,067 --> 00:20:55,833
If we get kicked out of here...

415
00:20:56,633 --> 00:20:59,000
...we wouldn't know
where to go.

416
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:05,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

417
00:21:06,800 --> 00:21:07,867
Don't worry.

418
00:21:09,133 --> 00:21:10,200
I'm here.

419
00:21:10,933 --> 00:21:12,100
I'll help you.

420
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:17,800
Gabo!

421
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:19,100
- Gabo!
- Gabo!

422
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:22,600
- Gabo! Gabo!
- Gabo!

423
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:25,200
[BABOT] Gabo! Gabo, it's Babot!

424
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:26,700
[KIDS] Gabo!

425
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:29,167
Pa, I'll meet Babot for a while.

426
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:32,633
Wait, can you manage?
I'll go with you.

427
00:21:33,633 --> 00:21:35,733
- Alright. [GRUNTS]
- Excuse me.

428
00:21:42,033 --> 00:21:44,633
Betchay almost put us
in danger.

429
00:21:44,633 --> 00:21:48,333
We thought Betchay
would be our hope,

430
00:21:48,333 --> 00:21:49,867
that, in a way,
she'd bring us money.

431
00:21:49,867 --> 00:21:54,133
In reality, she'll bring
Ginintuang Lupa to ruin.

432
00:21:54,133 --> 00:21:57,500
This is why
we cannot trust Betchay!

433
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,333
That woman's brain
is wired differently.

434
00:21:59,333 --> 00:22:01,067
But Rudy...

435
00:22:01,067 --> 00:22:04,900
Could it be that Betchay
also did not know?

436
00:22:05,833 --> 00:22:08,133
Maybe she's a victim too.

437
00:22:10,167 --> 00:22:11,200
I don't know.

438
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:15,333
[BABOT] Gabo!

439
00:22:15,367 --> 00:22:17,900
We just stopped by
to say thanks.

440
00:22:17,967 --> 00:22:20,367
We didn't get to thank you
last night.

441
00:22:20,367 --> 00:22:22,967
Yeah, we forgot
to thank you last night.

442
00:22:22,967 --> 00:22:24,133
Thank you, Gabo.

443
00:22:24,133 --> 00:22:27,533
[KIDS] Thank you, Gabo!

444
00:22:27,533 --> 00:22:29,133
You don't have to thank me.

445
00:22:29,133 --> 00:22:30,867
I just did
what I knew was right.

446
00:22:30,867 --> 00:22:34,733
- Gabo, are you okay now?
- Does it still hurt?

447
00:22:35,433 --> 00:22:38,133
I'm fine.
This is just a bit of pain.

448
00:22:38,133 --> 00:22:41,667
- Well, Gabo, who is she?
- Yeah, who is she?

449
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:45,233
Uh...

450
00:22:46,133 --> 00:22:47,600
M-My wife.

451
00:22:47,600 --> 00:22:49,233
- Really?
- Really?

452
00:22:49,267 --> 00:22:51,367
- Your wife?
- Your wife?

453
00:22:51,367 --> 00:22:54,033
[BOKBOK] Gabo, since when
did you have a wife?

454
00:22:55,433 --> 00:22:56,767
It's been a while.

455
00:22:57,433 --> 00:22:59,967
Back when I was still
in prison.

456
00:22:59,967 --> 00:23:02,067
- Ahh!
- Ahh!

457
00:23:02,067 --> 00:23:04,033
That's why we haven't seen her.

458
00:23:04,033 --> 00:23:05,300
- Yeah.
- So that's why.

459
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:07,533
Miss, what's your name?

460
00:23:08,900 --> 00:23:10,333
My name is Gloria.

461
00:23:10,333 --> 00:23:13,800
What a beautiful name!
It suits you!

462
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,600
- I'm Bilog!
- [CHUCKLES]

463
00:23:16,600 --> 00:23:20,200
- I'm Hopia!
- I'm Palits!

464
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:22,567
And I'm Bokbok!

465
00:23:23,333 --> 00:23:24,900
I'm Kulot!

466
00:23:25,667 --> 00:23:28,633
- Have you eaten?
- Not yet.

467
00:23:28,633 --> 00:23:31,967
- Would you like to eat?
- Yes!

468
00:23:33,733 --> 00:23:38,633
Love, you should treat them
to a barbecue,

469
00:23:38,633 --> 00:23:41,533
- so that the kids can eat.
- Sure.

470
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:47,300
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

471
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:50,600
- Let's go.
- Yay!

472
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:52,733
Go and eat!

473
00:23:52,733 --> 00:23:54,833
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

474
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:57,100
- Thank you very much, Gabo!
- Thank you!

475
00:23:57,133 --> 00:23:59,467
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

476
00:23:59,467 --> 00:24:01,167
Go ahead, pick what you like!

477
00:24:01,167 --> 00:24:02,200
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

478
00:24:02,200 --> 00:24:05,600
- Can we buy bread?
- Of course! Here.

479
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:07,833
- Give it to the vendor.
- Thank you.

480
00:24:07,833 --> 00:24:10,467
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

481
00:24:10,467 --> 00:24:14,200
Babot, how was last night?
Where are the men we fought?

482
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:15,533
No one's seen them, Gabo.

483
00:24:15,533 --> 00:24:18,567
But my neighbors said
they're still here, just hiding.

484
00:24:19,767 --> 00:24:23,567
That means we're still
in a dangerous situation.

485
00:24:23,567 --> 00:24:26,433
Gabo, could it be that they're
the ones harvesting organs?

486
00:24:26,433 --> 00:24:27,400
The ones who kidnapped me?

487
00:24:28,133 --> 00:24:29,167
I don't know yet.

488
00:24:32,367 --> 00:24:33,567
How's your injury?

489
00:24:33,567 --> 00:24:36,667
It still hurts.
I still can't move my shoulder.

490
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,633
Mister Kulas!

491
00:24:39,633 --> 00:24:42,233
Could you massage
Babot's sprain?

492
00:24:43,733 --> 00:24:45,933
Gabo, who's getting the massage?

493
00:24:45,933 --> 00:24:48,200
[GABO] Ah, Miss Diday,
it's Babot.

494
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:51,167
- He got sprained last night.
- Gabo, are you sure?

495
00:24:51,167 --> 00:24:52,900
Does Mister Kulas really know
how to massage a sprain?

496
00:24:52,900 --> 00:24:55,000
- Go on!
- Ma! What's with you?

497
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,933
Papa didn't even finish
his training

498
00:24:56,933 --> 00:24:58,067
- in traditional massage.
- He can do it!

499
00:24:58,067 --> 00:25:00,133
Else he'd massage other people.

500
00:25:00,133 --> 00:25:01,600
He went to class
for just one day!

501
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:02,900
That's fine!

502
00:25:02,933 --> 00:25:04,667
Gabo, what if
the sprain worsens?

503
00:25:04,667 --> 00:25:06,633
- [GABO] No, no.
- You sure?

504
00:25:06,633 --> 00:25:07,867
I studied this!

505
00:25:07,867 --> 00:25:12,200
- Where does it hurt? Here?
- Here. Yes, that hurts.

506
00:25:12,200 --> 00:25:14,700
- Give me a towel!
- Here, here!

507
00:25:15,333 --> 00:25:19,967
Straighten your arm,
so it doesn't get dislocated.

508
00:25:19,967 --> 00:25:21,767
Oh, oh, open your mouth.

509
00:25:21,767 --> 00:25:23,033
- Why?
- Open your mouth!

510
00:25:23,033 --> 00:25:25,233
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]
- Hold him down!

511
00:25:25,233 --> 00:25:27,700
Babot, don't worry!
Mister Kulas is good!

512
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:30,133
[KULAS] One, two, three!

513
00:25:30,133 --> 00:25:31,600
- [FLESH STRETCHES]
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]

514
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:33,967
[KULAS] One, two, three!

515
00:25:33,967 --> 00:25:36,933
- [MUFFLED SCREAMING]
- Once more!

516
00:25:36,967 --> 00:25:39,433
- [LAUGHING]
- [KULAS] Once more!

517
00:25:39,433 --> 00:25:40,500
- [BONE CRACKS]
- [BABOT GROANS]

518
00:25:42,033 --> 00:25:43,100
- Move!
- Oh my!

519
00:25:43,100 --> 00:25:44,900
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

520
00:25:44,900 --> 00:25:45,933
Hi, Django!

521
00:25:45,933 --> 00:25:47,533
- Here for a haircut?
- Where's Lala?

522
00:25:47,533 --> 00:25:48,567
She's inside.

523
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:50,367
Lala!

524
00:25:50,767 --> 00:25:54,000
Oh my gosh! Django!

525
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,133
Sit down.

526
00:25:55,133 --> 00:25:56,633
Marga, shampoo her hair.

527
00:25:56,633 --> 00:25:58,433
- It stinks. Hurry up!
- Okay.

528
00:25:58,433 --> 00:26:00,400
Django...
What brings you here?

529
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:01,967
Stop that, or I'll kick you.

530
00:26:01,967 --> 00:26:03,067
[INHALES DEEPLY]

531
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:04,967
So, what are you doing here?

532
00:26:04,967 --> 00:26:06,033
I need something from you.

533
00:26:06,033 --> 00:26:07,067
[GASPS]

534
00:26:07,067 --> 00:26:08,100
What?

535
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:10,267
Are you asking
for a second chance?

536
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:11,833
Do you want us
to get back together?

537
00:26:11,833 --> 00:26:14,300
And then you'll say,
"I've changed now."

538
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:16,800
But, no! Past is past!

539
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:18,633
I've had enough!

540
00:26:18,633 --> 00:26:20,833
Want me to yank
your teeth out with this?!

541
00:26:21,867 --> 00:26:23,433
Fine, what do you need?

542
00:26:25,433 --> 00:26:27,000
- I need a wig.
- A wig?

543
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:29,433
Oh my gosh.
Don't tell me.

544
00:26:29,433 --> 00:26:32,067
Don't tell me
you've switched sides now.

545
00:26:32,067 --> 00:26:33,400
Hey, FYI!

546
00:26:33,400 --> 00:26:35,067
Being gay is not contagious!

547
00:26:35,067 --> 00:26:36,033
Just because--

548
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:38,000
Want me to smash your face?!

549
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,067
Oh, Django...

550
00:26:39,067 --> 00:26:40,733
This is why I love you so much.

551
00:26:40,733 --> 00:26:43,467
I've missed all this
rough handling.

552
00:26:43,933 --> 00:26:45,433
- Do you have one or not?
- Oh!

553
00:26:45,433 --> 00:26:48,800
I do! What kind do you want?
I've got plenty here.

554
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:51,633
Long hair, short hair.
Whatever you need.

555
00:26:51,633 --> 00:26:52,767
You've got lots of options.

556
00:26:52,767 --> 00:26:53,900
That one.

557
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:55,000
This?

558
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:56,233
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

559
00:26:56,233 --> 00:26:57,200
Here.

560
00:26:58,733 --> 00:27:00,833
Hey, take care of that!
It's worth a lot.

561
00:27:00,833 --> 00:27:02,167
It came from a real...

562
00:27:02,167 --> 00:27:04,267
If I give that to you,
I'll stay alive.

563
00:27:04,267 --> 00:27:06,333
You've got no sense of humor.

564
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:08,533
[LALA] Come here!

565
00:27:09,367 --> 00:27:11,500
I'll shave your head clean!

566
00:27:11,500 --> 00:27:12,533
Boss Django.

567
00:27:12,533 --> 00:27:14,800
Is that enough to pin
the blame on Gabo?

568
00:27:14,800 --> 00:27:17,000
What else can identify Gabo?

569
00:27:17,033 --> 00:27:18,333
A motorcycle, boss.

570
00:27:18,333 --> 00:27:19,800
Isn't he always riding a bike?

571
00:27:19,800 --> 00:27:24,500
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

572
00:27:24,500 --> 00:27:25,533
[KEYPAD CLACKING]

573
00:27:26,700 --> 00:27:29,100
- [BIRDS CHIRPING]
- [LINE RINGING]

574
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:30,067
Hello, Pa?

575
00:27:30,067 --> 00:27:31,067
<i> Hello?</i>

576
00:27:31,067 --> 00:27:35,667
Boss Mariano's men
are on their way.

577
00:27:35,667 --> 00:27:37,533
<i> Wait for them at the entrance.</i>

578
00:27:37,533 --> 00:27:38,567
Yes, Pa.

579
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,467
By the way,
I need a motorcycle.

580
00:27:40,467 --> 00:27:41,400
Motorcycle?

581
00:27:41,400 --> 00:27:43,667
<i>I'll tell you later
where to send it.</i>

582
00:27:43,667 --> 00:27:45,500
I want one exactly like Gabo's.

583
00:27:46,067 --> 00:27:47,567
We're making an investment, Pa.

584
00:27:47,567 --> 00:27:49,433
I'll take care
of the motorcycle.

585
00:27:50,067 --> 00:27:51,567
Now, head over there.

586
00:27:51,567 --> 00:27:52,533
Yes, Pa.

587
00:27:52,533 --> 00:27:54,333
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

588
00:27:54,333 --> 00:27:55,300
[LOW CHUCKLE]

589
00:27:55,300 --> 00:27:56,267
Let's go.

590
00:27:57,600 --> 00:28:00,233
[WOMAN 1]
Gloria, you're so beautiful!

591
00:28:00,233 --> 00:28:01,733
What's your secret?

592
00:28:01,733 --> 00:28:05,133
At least share some tips
so I could be pretty like you.

593
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:07,633
- [WOMAN 1] Same here.
- Well, let me think...

594
00:28:08,167 --> 00:28:09,500
I would say...

595
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:12,167
a husband who takes good
care of you is important.

596
00:28:12,167 --> 00:28:13,267
[WOMAN 2] Mm-hmm.

597
00:28:13,267 --> 00:28:14,300
[WOMAN 1 CHUCKLES]

598
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:16,300
Uh, let me change the subject...

599
00:28:16,300 --> 00:28:18,033
Why the gratitude toward Gabo?

600
00:28:18,033 --> 00:28:19,467
What really happened last night?

601
00:28:19,467 --> 00:28:22,433
Listen, a group of armed men
came to my house.

602
00:28:22,467 --> 00:28:24,833
It was as if they were looking
for something.

603
00:28:25,333 --> 00:28:27,733
I have no idea
what it was, though.

604
00:28:27,733 --> 00:28:30,200
[WOMAN 2] Good thing
Gabo showed up and saved us.

605
00:28:30,200 --> 00:28:31,267
[WOMAN 1] That's true.

606
00:28:32,400 --> 00:28:34,167
You know, a long time ago...

607
00:28:34,167 --> 00:28:36,033
some men kidnapped my husband.

608
00:28:36,400 --> 00:28:39,533
They were members of that
organ-harvesting syndicate.

609
00:28:39,533 --> 00:28:42,567
Luckily, Gabo arrived
and rescued him.

610
00:28:42,567 --> 00:28:44,067
I was there.

611
00:28:44,067 --> 00:28:46,033
They really hurt us.

612
00:28:46,033 --> 00:28:48,100
They put black plastic bags
over our heads.

613
00:28:48,100 --> 00:28:49,500
They beat us up.

614
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:50,800
They even injected us with...

615
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:52,633
I don't know what it was,

616
00:28:52,633 --> 00:28:55,467
but it made us weak
ahead of the operation.

617
00:28:55,500 --> 00:28:57,267
We were lucky that Gabo came.

618
00:28:57,267 --> 00:28:58,333
He saved us.

619
00:28:58,333 --> 00:29:00,633
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

620
00:29:00,633 --> 00:29:03,067
[WOMAN 1] That's why
we owe Gabo so much.

621
00:29:04,500 --> 00:29:06,867
[SAM] <i> Now I'm getting
</i> to know you better.

622
00:29:07,733 --> 00:29:09,367
<i> You're actually kind.</i>

623
00:29:10,700 --> 00:29:13,567
<i>Genuinely humane
and loving toward others.</i>

624
00:29:15,300 --> 00:29:18,567
<i>I never imagined you were
this kind of person.</i>

625
00:29:18,567 --> 00:29:20,867
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

626
00:29:20,867 --> 00:29:22,967
<i> I had you all wrong.</i>

627
00:29:24,367 --> 00:29:25,933
<i> You've earned my admiration.</i>

628
00:29:35,967 --> 00:29:39,933
<i>We need to get back the gold
that NLEA took from us.</i>

629
00:29:39,933 --> 00:29:42,000
<i>It's getting too personal
for the team.</i>

630
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,767
<i> Form a new team.</i>

631
00:29:43,767 --> 00:29:46,900
<i>We can't halt the search
for Sam!</i>

632
00:29:46,900 --> 00:29:50,900
<i>I've never seen him this happy
since he was a young boy.</i>

633
00:29:50,900 --> 00:29:52,767
<i>If only things were real
between him and Gloria,</i>

634
00:29:52,767 --> 00:29:56,600
<i>I'd be the happiest father
in the world.</i>

635
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:58,800
<i> Love, I promise you this.</i>

636
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:01,500
<i>You're the only woman
I'll ever love.</i>
